scenario: TOUCH-02
title: Trackpad, keyboard and Touch Bar of a Mac laptop
area: Touch
rows: F-KBD-10, F-KBD-11, F-KBD-14
machines: macbook
needs: person
prereq: A MacBook, signed in, no external mouse.
step: Move one finger over the trackpad and press it down to click.
expect: The pointer moves smoothly and the click chooses what is under it.
clause: F-KBD-10.pointer
step: Type a line with every row of keys into any text field, including the number keys and the Fn row.
expect: Every key types the right character with no repeats or missing letters.
clause: F-KBD-10.keys
step: If the MacBook has a Touch Bar, look at it and hold Fn.
expect: The strip shows buttons and changes strips while Fn is held; if there is no Touch Bar write Cannot test for this step.
clause: F-KBD-14.strip
step: Press the brightness and volume keys.
expect: Each key changes what its symbol says.
clause: F-KBD-11.fnkeys
